---
import { ico } from '../../lib/icons';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How do you work with an in-house engineering team?',
    a: 'We work inside your setup, not alongside it — your repository, your branching model, your review process, your ticket tracker. On embedded engagements we join standups and take work off the same board your team does. The goal is that our commits are indistinguishable in process from anyone else on the team.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who owns the code and the intellectual property?',
    a: 'You do. All work is delivered as work-for-hire: the code, the infrastructure definitions, and the documentation are yours from the first commit. We are happy to work under your MSA, or to sign an NDA before the first technical call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you take over an existing codebase?',
    a: 'Yes, and a good part of the work we do is exactly that — inheriting systems, mapping what is actually there, and modernizing or extending them without a rewrite nobody asked for. The first deliverable in those cases is usually an honest assessment of the current state.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does the discovery engagement produce?',
    a: 'A written technical plan: the proposed architecture, how it fits the systems you already run, the sequence of work, the risks we see, and what it will cost. It is a standalone deliverable — you can take it to another vendor or build it internally, with no obligation to continue with us.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What technologies do you build with?',
    a: 'Primarily TypeScript, Python, and Go, with React and Angular on the front end and Node.js or FastAPI on the back. Infrastructure runs on AWS or GCP, defined as code with AWS CDK. When you already have a stack, we work in it rather than arguing for ours.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you handle security and compliance requirements?',
    a: 'They get treated as constraints on the architecture from day one, not as a review at the end. We have built in regulated contexts — including medical diagnostics — and are comfortable working under access controls, audit requirements, and customer security reviews.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How quickly can you start?',
    a: 'Discovery engagements can usually start within a week or two. Larger builds and embedded work depend on current commitments — the technical call is the fastest way to get a real answer on timing.',
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(f => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<section
  id='faq'
  class='px-5 sm:px-8 py-20 md:py-28'
  style='background-color: var(--color-surface-2);'
  aria-labelledby='faq-heading'
>
  <div class='mx-auto max-w-3xl'>
    <div class='text-center'>
      <p
        class='text-xs font-bold tracking-widest uppercase'
        style='color: var(--color-brand-blue);'
      >
        FAQ
      </p>
      <h2
        id='faq-heading'
        class='mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl'
        style='color: var(--color-brand-dark);'
      >
        Common questions
      </h2>
      <p
        class='mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed'
        style='color: var(--color-text-secondary);'
      >
        What engineering leaders and operators usually want settled before the first call.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='mt-10 space-y-3'>
      {
        faqs.map(f => (
          <details
            class='group rounded-2xl border'
            style='border-color: var(--color-border); background-color: var(--color-surface);'
          >
            <summary
              class='flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-base font-semibold sm:px-6'
              style='color: var(--color-brand-dark);'
            >
              {f.q}
              <span
                class='shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45'
                style='color: var(--color-brand-blue);'
                set:html={ico('plus')}
              />
            </summary>
            <p
              class='px-5 pb-5 text-sm leading-relaxed sm:px-6'
              style='color: var(--color-text-secondary);'
            >
              {f.a}
            </p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script
  type='application/ld+json'
  is:inline
  set:html={JSON.stringify(faqJsonLd)}
/>
